/theme/watch.ts` | watches `lang`; calls back synchronously per observer batch so the controller schedules its frame | existing theme tests; snapshot \"finding 19\" |\n    89\t| `src/theme/css.ts` (figure section) | stage, table overlay, readout, swatch dash, jump error, one-line summary | — |\n    90\t| `core/stages.ts`, `test/core/host.ts` | as granted | — |\n    91\t\n    92\tThe two changed expectations in `test/scene/scene.test.ts` belong to the scene module's author; they should review them.\n    93\t\n    94\t### Last lines of each run\n    95\t- **Type check:** `tsc -p packages/axylo` and `tsc -p docs/api` both clean.\n    96\t- **Node core:** `Tests 114 passed (114)`. Node acceptance: `Tests 494 passed (494)`.\n    97\t- **`npm test`:** `1 failed | 1209 passed`. The one failure is simplify's million-point timing test, not mine.\n    98\t- **Owned browser directories:** SVG `Tests 163 passed (163)`; canvas `Tests 163 passed (163)`.\n    99\t- **Browser acceptance:** SVG `Tests 5 failed | 452 passed (457)` (the five listed above).\n# Decision 0003: the default categorical palette\n\nStatus: **proposed, refitted after review.** The first version (commit 51e1be5) was reviewed by Codex gpt-6.2-astra (`reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/palette.review.md`). The review confirmed the arithmetic and showed four things wrong: the uneven lightness was claimed to be forced and is not; simulated screenshots and 8-bit fills fell below the limits the record promised; the order explorer could prune a feasible order after a timeout; and the record overclaimed in several places. This version is a refit with byte-level checks and corrected text. The hard constraints are measured and tested. Whether the result is good to look at is the owner's call (see \"For the owner\"). The refit itself has not been reviewed.\n\nSpec: A5 (palette thresholds, provisional), L2 (3:1 for marks), F9 (eight series). Finding R7, docs/01-landscape.md.\n\n## The palette\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"**The release gate can pass with required behavior removed.** The motion tests disable animations while measuring them. The table tests accept values under the wrong column headers. The reference tests accept a chart with neither reference mark drawn. The distribution suite also passes declarations that fail in a NodeNext TypeScript consumer.\n\nI reviewed `13b2f63` and `bf8fabf`, and checked the five residual failures against `77213c0`. I ran read-only Node, TypeScript, esbuild and font-measurement probes. I did not launch a browser or change files. Browser results below are attributed to the recorded runs.\n\n### Findings\n\n**B** means the test can be cited for a criterion it does not establish. **M** means a major limitation. **m** means a narrower defect.\n\n1. **B · I5 · Reasoned. The screenshot helper suppresses the behavior under test.** Every motion screenshot passes `animations: 'disabled'`. Playwright fast-forwards finite CSS animations and transitions. A one-second entry fade or a transition under reduced motion can therefore produce equal screenshots. `createRaw` also waits for readiness and three frames before the “first” capture. The update test waits two frames, allows another 300 ms, and never requires the updated picture to differ from the old one. An ignored update passes. Capture with animations enabled from the first eligible paint, require the known new data to appear, and measure the 200 ms deadline, including the specified 24-chart change. [Screenshot helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:246) · [Creation wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:72) · [Motion tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:419)\n\n2. **B · Packed TypeScript API · Ran. A supported ESM consumer loses the public types.** Both supplied Bundler-mode projects compile. Running the npm fixture with `--module NodeNext --moduleResolution NodeNext --noEmit` produces TS2834 at lines 5 and 6 of the shipped `index.d.ts`, missing public exports, and unused `@ts-expect-error` directives. The React fixture also loses its core option types. The `types` condition is correctly first and `public.d.ts` ships. The failure is the extensionless `./public` inside the ESM declaration. Emit `./public.js` in those declaration references and compile minimal packed consumers in both resolution modes. [Public entry](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:5) · [Fixture configuration](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/fixtures/npm/tsconfig.json:3) · [Type tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/types.test.ts:13)\n\n3. **B · DX7/P6 · Ran. The size measurement is reproducible, but CI succeeds over budget.** I recovered the original tarball from the local npm cache, verified its SHA-512 against the committed size record, and independently bundled its production ESM bytes with esbuild `write:false`. Everything measured **283,389 minified bytes, 100,093 gzip bytes, 97.75 KiB**. Line-only measured **282,947 / 99,956 / 97.61 KiB**. CI calls `size` without `--check`. Even with `--check`, the script compares rounded KiB, so 40 KiB plus one byte passes. Compare integer bytes against `targetKiB * 1024` and make that exit status part of the release gate. The later fixture currently on disk gives 98.44 KiB and has a different integrity hash. [Size comparison](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/size.mjs:64) · [CI invocation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/.github/workflows/ci.yml:44) · [Recorded artifact](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/bench/size-latest.json:4)\n\n4. **B · L2/A5 · Ran the colour math, reasoned about the browser assertions. The palette test measures CSS colours before painting.** `seriesColors` takes the first computed `color` per SVG slot and fills a separate one-pixel canvas with it. The background comes from a CSS variable. Making the marks nearly transparent, changing their actual fill, or covering them leaves those readings intact. L2 similarly walks ancestor background colours, misses a mark painted behind text, and can pass an empty axis-colour loop. The severity-1 Machado coefficients, sRGB decoding, linear-RGB multiplication, clamp and OKLab transform are correct. My primary-colour and white probes matched reference OKLab values. The helper computes the continuous result and omits the simulated-image byte rounding distinguished in decision 0003. Sample known mark interiors and their actual backdrops in both schemes, assert samples exist, and score both analytic and raster variants. [Palette test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:294) · [Colour source](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:276) · [L2](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:100) · [Math](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/vision.ts:11)\n\n5. **B · A5 · Ran the separator counterexample, reasoned about grayscale. Both perceptual thresholds can give false passes.** I fed `separated` a transition with 0.80 pixel of background coverage. It reported one transition and zero touching. Stacked bars have an additional geometry check. Grouped bars, areas and donuts lack that protection, and the four-slice test accepts three transitions, missing the closing seam. The 85% marker intersection-over-union threshold is invented. Identical shapes can produce different thresholded masks through luminance, subpixel alignment or nearby ink. Check a full CSS pixel normal to each boundary, including the closing seam, and calibrate raster tolerance with known-width controls. For grayscale, include identical-shape negative controls and verify that the crossing traces can be matched to their legend markers. [Coverage calculation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:178) · [Closing seam](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:265) · [Marker masks](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:335)\n\n6. **B · L1/L8/A6 · Ran the text helper, reasoned about layout. A chart can discard labels and still pass.** Removing date or numeric ticks leaves fewer boxes to collide. Only the bar fixture compares a category count. The suite does not establish remedy order, three-line wrapping, the rotation limit, middle truncation with recoverable full text, AX143’s suggestion, or unchanged orientation. I confirmed that two boxes overlapping by 1.1 px are ignored when they have the same owner. Tooltip/readout text is excluded. L8 accepts a visible multi-line summary and does not bracket the 120×80 plot boundary. A6 uses a 320 px Chrome viewport as the 400% proxy and checks spacing separately. Use generated labels with known identities, check clipping ancestors and the actual remedies, bracket the fallback dimensions, and repeat with browser zoom and a delayed font in the required engines. A sibling test already loads an offline font. [L1](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:49) · [Text exclusions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/text.ts:20) · [L8](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:419) · [A6](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:49) · [Offline font precedent](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts:439)\n\n7. **B · I1 and pointer/tooltip cells · Reasoned. Late, obscuring or incomplete tooltips can pass.** Every probe settles before reading, so there is no input-to-paint p95 measurement. Scatter and donut supply `marks: []`, making their pointer occlusion assertion vacuous. Bars check only the top eight pixels. The hover test jumps into the tooltip and checks visibility without checking that the same datum stayed put. The narrow readout can drop all eight rows and retain `+2 more`. A scatter radius of 20 px can pass the tested inside offsets and 30 px miss. Exercise a slow pointer path, hit-test the tooltip, check the active mark and all row identities on both surfaces, bracket 24 px, and reverse source order in the tie fixture. Add horizontal bars, hidden area/bar series, and timestamped paints. [Pointer probes](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:37) · [Hover and readout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:99) · [Scatter radius](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:88)\n\n8. **B · A1/A4 · Ran the text oracle, reasoned about the table. Correct words can be attached to the wrong thing.** Swapping North and South’s cells while retaining their headers passes `toContain` for each value. Missing scatter series and donut category/percentage headers can pass the header subset check. The range test omits zoomable bars, and the layout test uses two fixed-height charts instead of the specified 24. For A1, I passed every compact summary-fragment assertion with the overall range statement removed. With an author description, retaining only that text, the zone and the omission also passes. Compare ordered headers and exact ordered cell arrays, assert each named summary clause, and check a date-bar zoom and a 24-tile layout. The fixture formatter also turns `0.000123456` into `0.000123`, contrary to F6. Use hand-written boundary values. [Table expectations](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a4-table.browser.test.ts:86) · [Range cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a4-table.browser.test.ts:207) · [Summary assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a1-names.browser.test.ts:104) · [Fixture formatter](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/fixtures.ts:21)\n\n9. **B · A2/A7 and keyboard evidence · Reasoned. The tests can keep reading the old proxy after focus has gone elsewhere.** `valueText` reads the selected DOM element’s `aria-valuetext`. It never requires that element to be focused or exposed as a range. The focus-indicator test compares the tooltip with datum marks rather than the indicator. The streaming test uses a growing window while focused, strips position and donut percentage in one comparison, and omits donut from the stricter check. A stale proxy, a covered ring, or lost focus at eviction can pass. Assert the active element, its unignored AX role, numeric position and bounds, actual ring clearance, and the next navigation result before and after eviction. Keep the DOM value-text assertion explicitly labelled. [Value-text helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:182) · [Focus indicator](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a2-keyboard.browser.test.ts:246) · [Streaming focus](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:131)\n\n10. **B · L7/A7/I6 · Reasoned. State changes can reach the reader while the checked surface stays quiet.** L7 verifies one nonempty polite mutation on loading→ready. An unrelated announcement qualifies. Error and internal-failure messages need only differ or be nonempty, with no equivalent bounds, tick or announcement checks. A7’s observer misses a newly inserted, already populated alert whose parent is outside a live region. I6 freezes only SVG scene markup and checks a final row count. While paused, the summary, lookup or open table could advance, or Resume could duplicate one buffered row and lose another. Assert exact state text, geometry and notification sequence, and compare fixture values across the reader surfaces during pause and after resume. [State transitions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:383) · [Live observer](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:97) · [Pause test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:477)\n\n11. **B · A8 · Reasoned. “Every fixture in every state” exceeds what axe scanned.** The helper requests all default-enabled rules with no explicit rule disablement. Most runs are scoped to `#chart`. The additional `body` run retains only `heading-order`, and the suite discards `incomplete` results without requiring `scrollable-region-focusable` to complete. Hidden scatter series, paused charts, zoomed bars, compact area/bar and other fixtures are absent. The pointer-tooltip setup can also miss a scatter point or land in the donut hole without failing setup. Assert each state exists before scanning, enumerate applicable fixture/state pairs, and record completion of the named rules. Use a page with suitable landmarks for the document-level scan. [State selection and axe results](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:166) · [Axe configuration](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:117)\n\n12. **B · A10 · Ran the key comparison, reasoned about coverage. “Every built-in string” has a concrete omission.** `seeTable` exists in the reviewed contract and is absent from `MESSAGE_KEYS` and the replacement placeholders. One `ZZ-` anywhere plus the absence of a short English blacklist is enough. Hard-coding `Resume`, for example, passes without entering the paused state. At `77213c0` the language test inspects `.axylo-summary`, while the figure actually references `.axylo-description`. Removing `lang` only from the referenced description can pass. Use a compile-time exhaustive message map, trigger each applicable string, and require its individual sentinel and language at the surface that exposes it. [Replacement and language tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:215) · [Public message](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/public.ts:204) · [Referenced description](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:200)\n\n13. **B · T-dense/C2 · Reasoned. A spike at the wrong x passes the dense line and area tests.** Both use one unstacked series and compare the globally highest stroke coordinate with a height calculated from the library’s own domain. Moving the spike to another column or drawing every sample passes. No cumulative stack, same-column break, dropped-but-reachable ordinary sample, DPR variation or compact simplification is established. The scatter test counts `M` commands and the donut test counts paths, so repeated geometry can stand in for missing marks. Derive expected per-column extrema and breaks from fixture coordinates at a fixed domain, check stacked cumulative values, and identify marks by location. [Dense tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:294) · [Compact fidelity cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts:78)\n\n14. **B · T-limit/F8 · Reasoned. The ninth series can reuse the first cue, and the wrong seven slices can be selected.** The test computes drawn identities but asserts only `drawn.length >= 9`. Multiple elements of one series count separately. Distinct legend SVG markup does not prove distinct painted cues. Every grouping fixture places the seven largest values first, so keeping the first seven passes. The ordinary order fixture is also descending, and the all-zero test accepts an arbitrary nonempty error message. Check eight without the limit warning and nine with it, associate one painted cue with each series, scramble slice magnitudes, and compare the exact grouped arc, legend, table and empty state. [Identity assertion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:404) · [Donut grouping and empty state](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts:101)\n\n15. **B · L6/T-reference · Reasoned. Removing the reference drawing passes.** The four Cartesian cases verify a domain, label near a calculated line position, and words in the summary and caption. They never require the line or band to be painted. The band is inside the data extent, and its adjacent label is unchecked. The donut negative case likewise checks the label, description and diagnostic without inspecting for an unintended mark. Put each reference outside the original extent in turn, sample its geometry or pixels, and check each label against its own mark. [Reference cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:429)\n\n16. **B · F2/F12 · Reasoned. Comparing two renderings can preserve the same gap bug, and a changed-value note can say the wrong thing.** For regular dates, bridging both the null run and the deleted run passes the geometry-equality check. The rendered suite never requests `missing: 'zero'`. Scatter counts two marks without identifying them or checking the missing row in the table. The donut F2 body only reads the table. For changed values, `1 … table` satisfies the AX160 case without checking AX160 or the meaning of the note. The AX121 case likewise accepts a note saying the grouped values were lost. Assert independent gap/zero coordinates, the affected rows, the diagnostic, and exact changed-versus-omitted wording at the displayed revision. [Date gaps](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts:74) · [Scatter and donut](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts:144) · [Changed-value notes](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts:89)\n\n17. **B · I2/I3/I4 · Reasoned. Several control paths can be disabled independently.** Space need only change AX `pressed`, with no post-Space mark check. Zoom out is never clicked, Meta-wheel is absent, and the default pinch can suppress browser zoom while leaving the chart domain unchanged. I4 measures visible buttons and inputs. Selectable tooltip rows are `div` elements and never enter that measurement. Touch exercises a datum and page scroll, leaving most controls unoperated by touch. Assert each control’s visible result with its actual input, check browser defaults and both modifiers, and measure clickable tooltip rows while displayed. Donut and compact are appropriately outside the series-toggle matrix. [Legend tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:200) · [Zoom and touch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:307) · [Selectable rows](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:89)\n\n18. **B · L3/L4/L5 · Reasoned. The layout and theme observations permit stale marks.** L3 can resize the CSS box while retaining the old drawing, and never opens the auto-height table to check flow. L4’s dark fixture sets both scheme and text colour, so always choosing by text luminance can pass. It permits two animation frames and lacks independent runtime checks for the specified root attributes and media changes. L5 samples roughly 5.5 px and widely separated points. A 20 px cutoff can pass both. Check a known datum and hit target across resizes, open the table, deliberately put scheme and inherited colour in conflict, measure the first post-change paint, and bracket 12 px. [L3](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:159) · [L4](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:218) · [L5](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:281)\n\n19. **B · C1–C5 · Reasoned. Compact coverage does not transfer across implementations of the three variants.** The general `compact` fixture is a line. Disabling motion or theme updates only on compact area/bar escapes those loops. C1’s hover check only searches for two named surfaces on one tile. C2’s area can fill from a truncated domain minimum to the bottom and pass the vertical-extent check. C3 checks SVG dimensions and the existence of a series element, allowing stale internal geometry. C4 reads cues on the coloured group and misses child paint. C5’s signed corner distances accept a marker entirely outside the figure. Parameterize the relevant fixtures over all three kinds. Verify marks-only behavior, data-derived geometry at each size, child paint, the AX131 suggestion, and a visible corner marker contained within the figure. [Compact fixture](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/fixtures.ts:105) · [C1/C2](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts:54) · [C3/C4/C5](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts:130)\n\n20. **B · DX8 text insertion · Reasoned. The same payload in several fields lets one surface vouch for another.** Full visible titles get exact comparisons. Series names, categories, subtitle, field labels, units, tick and value formatters receive payloads, and a document observer detects the selected element types if inserted. But tooltip positives cover only line/bar, the line name can satisfy its formatter assertion, and a table caption can satisfy the whole-table regex while cells are blank. Area has no table-text positive assertion. There is no per-tick, per-unit, summary or exact `aria-*` assertion. Messages overrides and a dirty reader note are never exercised. Use a different inert markup-shaped sentinel for each source, trigger each destination, and assert exact literal text or attribute value plus absence of parsed descendants. [Inputs](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/pages/charts.ts:21) · [Surface assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts:92) · [Observer](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/pages/observe.js:9)\n\n21. **B · DX8 StrictMode and DX1 scope · Reasoned. A leaked first mount can leave the expected single figure.** The React fixture really enables development StrictMode, but the assertion sees only the eventual figure. Keeping the original subscription or observer alive through cleanup can pass. Observe setup, disposal, setup again and final unmount through the packed adapter, including whether the old handle still acts. The DX1 snippets demonstrate a first **line** chart by all three routes. Only npm is exercised without a title. A matrix that repeats those results for the other constructors needs corresponding minimal examples or an explicit package-level scope. DX10 coverage here ends at those three snippets. [StrictMode test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:113) · [Untitled test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:49) · [Snippet inventory](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/snippets.test.ts:13)\n\n22. **M · Fixture isolation and extraction · Ran resolution and archive probes.** Normal core imports resolve inside each fixture, and the React fixture resolves both packed packages. But the npm and script fixtures can import undeclared `@axylo/react` from root `node_modules`. I observed Node resolve `packages/react/dist/index.js`, esbuild pull in workspace React **and core source**, and TypeScript resolve an explicit adapter type reference to `packages/react/dist/index.d.ts`. The existing positive path checks catch several fallbacks in their specific projects. They do not isolate consumers. Put fixtures outside the workspace ancestry and share only declared third-party dependencies. The actual archives contained 10 and 6 regular files, with no links or extended names. The extractor handles ordinary ustar prefixes, GNU `L`, and simple local pax `path=` records. Splitting pax by newline breaks a length-prefixed path containing a newline, global headers are ignored, and symlinks are rejected. npm’s packlist excludes ordinary symlinks. Prefer the npm installation/extraction path or explicitly constrain and test the supported subset. [Fixture placement and extraction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/pack.mjs:42) · [Isolation assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/isolation.test.ts:29) · [Type path checks](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/types.test.ts:33)\n\n23. **M · CSP observation · Reasoned. All eight pages have the instruments, but report attribution and style-effect checks are incomplete.** The actual HTTP header meets DX8. The external observer loads before chart code in all four loaders × two stylesheet modes. The negative page requires both script-attribute and style-attribute events, an observed element, blocked execution and at least one POST. It does not match the two reports to those directives. A shared report array is cleared between tests and sampled after 300 ms, so a late POST can be lost or attributed to the next page. Counted adopted sheets can also be empty. Use a per-page report URL, correlate the negative reports by directive/document, and assert a characteristic computed rule and painted result. The linked sheets are same-origin, and constructable sheets and CSSOM assignments are legitimate Chrome paths here. I found no inline stylesheet silently allowed on the eight pages. The documented CDN example has an inline bootstrap and is exercised separately without this header. [Policy and page setup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts:52) · [Report sampling and control](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts:127) · [HTTP server](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/browser.ts:36) · [Documented example](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/examples/first-chart/script.html:6)\n\n24. **M · Distribution oracles · Reasoned. Two tests derive their assurance from what the current source happens to contain.** Removing a development guard makes its body disappear from the guard-derived token oracle, while other detected tokens can keep the check green. The licence test treats finding a copyright header as failure and accepts a notice document that says there is no third-party code. Vendored code without a header passes, and properly attributed code fails. Pin observable development-only behavior independently of the guard syntax. Verify the release inventory and corresponding notices, retaining the mechanical checks for the shipped MIT file, dependencies and imports. [Development token oracle](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/conditions.test.ts:142) · [Licence assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/licence.test.ts:68)\n\n### Disposition of the 14 recorded failures\n\n| Original failures | Judgment from the recorded output and source |\n|---|---|\n| **A10, six types** | **Original product defect.** Built-in English summary sentences inherited German. The later figure code sets a language on both summary elements, and all six pass in the later run. Finding 12 limits what those passes establish. [Figure update](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:200) |\n| **A5, grouped bar** | **Original product defect under the ordinary reading of “adjacent filled marks.”** At the original revision each bar consumed the full group subdivision, leaving zero geometric gap. The reported 0.22 px is consistent with antialiasing at a touching edge. The later revision subtracts a pixel and the fixture passes. [Grouped widths](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:70) |\n| **C4, compact bar** | **Original product gap under A5; residual test defect at `77213c0`.** C4 literally specifies dashes for lines. Requiring a non-colour cue for compact bars is supported by A5. Originally neither of the first two series received a pattern. At `77213c0` the second does, and SVG paints it on child rectangles. The test skips children without their own inline series colour and compares `none\\|\\|` with `none\\|\\|`. Inspect the child fills or pixels before treating this as a product failure. [Pattern selection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:106) · [SVG paint](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:410) |\n| **L1, line/area/scatter/donut at 200% text** | **Original product defects. Residual reader-visible clipping, with a misleading test diagnosis.** The original output includes full summaries and displaced controls. The later run reports only the first sentence at 240 px. The stylesheet now ellipsizes it, while `Range.getClientRects()` measures the underlying text. That output cannot establish painted ink outside the figure or vertical overflow. Independently, the four sentences measured **270, 276, 303 and 288 px** in local Noto Sans at the fixture’s 24.5 px summary size. Each exceeds 240 px. Under L1/L8 I would retain the reader-facing failure until a meaningful one-line summary fits, and change the test to distinguish clipping, ellipsis and actual overflow. [Summary CSS](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:122) · [Range measurement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/text.ts:36) |\n| **I1, scatter** | **Original product defect.** The recorded misses include a probe inside the plot near the top-edge EU point. `43fc75d` corrected edge projection and grid-cell rounding. The later acceptance run passes. [Grid boundary handling](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:47) |\n| **I1, bar** | **Original product defect.** Seven in-viewport top-row probes produced a reader surface outside the viewport. That directly violates I1. The later placement changes pass this fixture. [Viewport assertion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:82) · [Later run report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:73) |\n\n### Accessibility, input and waits\n\n**Computed Chrome AX evidence** comes from `Accessibility.getPartialAXTree` and `getFullAXTree`. It covers A1 names/descriptions/heading levels, I2 pressed state, A4 table roles/names/rows/cells and region focusability, F12 note text, C1/C5 image descriptions, and parts of F2, F8, L7, L8, T-reference and A10. **DOM evidence** includes A2/T-keyboard/F2/A7 `aria-valuetext`, live-region mutation counts, nearest `lang` ancestors, and part of the jump-error description check. Those establish authoring or DOM behavior. They do not establish speech. The distribution `figureName` helper uses Playwright’s `ariaSnapshot`, a different mechanism from the CDP tree helper. [AX helpers](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:138) · [Distribution name helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/browser.ts:166)\n\nI found **no DOM-dispatched synthetic pointer, touch, wheel or keyboard events** in the reviewed acceptance tests. Playwright supplies mouse, keyboard and tap input. Pinch and one-finger scroll use CDP `Input.dispatchTouchEvent`, which exercises Chrome’s input pipeline. Direct `.focus()` bypasses the route to focus, and `chart.zoom()` establishes state without exercising a reader control. Those are appropriate setup operations only when the route itself has separate evidence. Touch emulation provides no physical-phone or touch-screen-reader result. [Pinch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:307) · [Touch scroll](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:385)\n\nI found **no timeout-to-skip path**. The catches after the F12 note, L3 reveal and I4 scroll waits are followed by assertions that fail if the state remains absent. They do allow a transient or substantially delayed success, and I4 should compare the post-drag scroll position with its immediate pre-drag position. The consequential timing loopholes are the multi-frame settle, disabled animations, and the longer observation deadlines. [Note wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts:91) · [Reveal wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:205) · [Scroll wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:400)\n\n### The report’s ambiguity choices\n\n| Reading | Judgment |\n|---|---|\n| Space before unit; medium en-US dates | Reasonable English fixture conventions. The spec permits locale-appropriate presentation. The six-fractional-places helper is a separate error. |\n| Summary y range means observed data extrema | Appropriate for a reader asking what values occurred. Test an axis whose bounds differ from the data and require an identifiable range statement. |\n| Scatter “last” means greatest x | Consistent with x-ordered navigation. Use shuffled input and define the equal-x case. |\n| Donut summary gives each value and share | Appropriate for parts of a whole. Also cover grouping, omissions and zero/null slices. |\n| Unmatched table jump gets a visible error | Appropriate. Require the error to identify the field and be programmatically associated with it. |\n| Separator coverage ≥0.75 px | Lowers the explicit 1 px requirement. Antialiasing calls for calibration, not a smaller nominal gap. |\n| Grayscale overlap ≤85% | An unvalidated regression heuristic. It cannot decide whether a reader can follow the crossing lines. |\n| A focused range should not recount arrivals | Consistent with decision 0004 for an unchanged datum. DOM stability is measurable; actual announcements require rehearsal. |\n| AX160 and AX121 count as “changed” | AX121 changes the displayed grouping. AX160 changes the presentation of a value. A disclosure is defensible in both cases, with wording that explains what changed and preserves the distinction from lost data. |\n| Double the inherited font size for text-only zoom | Useful for reproducing a real layout defect. It leaves fixed-pixel text unchanged and cannot substitute for browser text zoom. |\n| Hover the tooltip in one pointer step | Lowers the bar. A reader must be able to move onto it continuously and keep the same content. Decision 0004 explicitly describes that path. |\n| Scatter x-only zoom preserves the y domain | A reasonable 1.0 reading. Confirm the displayed y ticks against a fixture whose visible y extrema change materially. |\n| Allow 300 ms for a 200 ms transition | Lowers the explicit deadline by 50%, before the initial frame waits and screenshot overhead. |\n\n### Type-matrix disposition\n\nThese judgments cover the tested default SVG renderer. A later canvas run had 135 failures, many arising from SVG-specific inspection. It supplies no equivalent canvas pass. [Renderer report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:99)\n\n| Cell | Line | Area | Bar | Donut | Scatter |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pointer picking | Nearest-x fixture established | Same | Vertical bands only | Slice, hole and outside exercised | 24 px boundary and tie independence open |\n| Tooltip content | Visible/hidden fixture established | Initial stack total only | Grouped fixture only | Label/value/share established | Coincident row identities open |\n| Keyboard order | Fixture ordinal text exercised | Same | Same for vertical categories | Slice order exercised | x-then-y order exercised |\n| Zoom | Positive zoom exercised | Positive zoom exercised | Category/date covered; numeric and instant eligibility open | Keys tested in a sequence that can cancel; check after each action | x-only domain behavior exercised |\n| Dense drawing | Per-column F5 open | Cumulative F5 open | Count and AX132 exercised | Path count only | Count and AX133 exercised; positions and slow-drawing advice open |\n| Limit | Nine-warning positive only | Same | Same | Sorted-only grouping; boundary open | Nine-warning positive only |\n| Reference | Geometry and band domain open | Same | Same | Rejection/text checked; unintended drawing unchecked | Geometry and band domain open |\n\nThe fixture values and basic arithmetic generally have identifiable sources. I found no basis for alleging that the author pasted browser output. The problematic oracles are identifiable without that allegation: sibling-derived geometry, equality between two potentially wrong outputs, development tokens inferred from current source, and fragment/count assertions that discard associations.\n\n### Verification and areas found sound\n\nMy five read-only Node checks exercised OKLab reference colours, same-owner overlap, compact summary fragments, fractional formatting and separator coverage. The last lines were:\n\n```text\nℹ tests 5\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 5\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\n```\n\nThe recorded browser totals were `14 failed | 443 passed (457)` originally and `5 failed | 452 passed (457)` at the later revision. I did not rerun either browser suite or the dist global setup, which replaces fixture directories. No contract change is needed for the test fixes. [Original report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/acceptance-browser.report.md) · [Later report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:94)\n\n- **Colour arithmetic — ran.** Normal-vision OKLab reference values matched, and the severity-1 simulation uses the expected matrices and linear-light ordering.\n- **Input injection — reasoned.** The real-key, mouse, wheel and CDP touch paths are appropriate for the Chrome interactions they actually exercise.\n- **Table paging — reasoned.** All 250 row headers are compared across three pages, and the million-row line fixture independently expects `123.25` at x `900,123`.\n- **Node import and validation — ran.** Both packed core conditions loaded without a DOM, added no globals, and returned AX103 at row 3, AX106 at row 4 and AX102 at row 5.\n- **CSP delivery — reasoned.** All eight variants receive the strict response header and early event listener. The negative control exercises blocked inline script-attribute and style-attribute paths.\n- **Package metadata — ran and inspected.** The `files` lists include the required entries and current declaration closure. `types` precedes runtime conditions. `[\"*.css\"]` correctly preserves CSS as a bundler side effect, and the adapter’s `sideEffects: false` is consistent with its import behavior. The esbuild CSS test alone cannot validate webpack behavior.\n- **Download accounting — ran.** Browser ESM, ES2022, production/default export selection, esbuild minification and gzip level 9 reproduce the figures. Bundler rows count embedded CSS once. The documented script-tag page downloads both its JS and linked CSS, so counting both transfers is correct. The adapter-only figure excludes its peers.\n\n**Criteria I would leave open for at least one applicable type:** **L1–L8, I1–I6, A1, A2, A4–A8, A10, F2 rendered, F5 rendered, F8, F12, C1–C5**, and the partial type-matrix cells identified above. On distribution, **DX7/P6 fails its measured budgets; DX8 and DX11 are partial; DX1 is established only at the demonstrated first-chart scope; DX10 beyond the three snippets is open.** A3 and A9 were outside this review."}}
